  "qualification": "Five complete source rows per profile (zero, minute/hour components, more than one day, negative) retain numeric values and mapped formats; 21 native C+C formulas and their typed caches survive saved/reopened XLSX and local recalculation. All 42 mapped format codes and native day-serial caches agree with Apple XLSX. Integral shared display agrees with native Numbers PDF. Fractional and destination-application display remain approximated.",
  "knownLimits": [
    "Numbers rounds fractional source seconds; the shared elapsed formatter can truncate them. Raw values and formula caches are retained, and duration display approximation is reported.",
    "Native Excel renders the Apple XLSX hour/second and minute/second negative cells as hashes; the observed seconds-only negatives are displayed. Fractional display differs between Numbers, Excel and the shared formatter. The screenshots qualify only the recorded values and versions.",
    "Synthetic Pages/Keynote table and blank-format cases prove adapter behavior; this native reference is a Numbers fixture. Other label styles, automatic units, milliseconds, locale and unit ranges remain unqualified.",
    "This reference does not qualify exact composed PDF geometry, typography, other producers, sandbox hosts or published packages."
  ],
